---
smd: 2
title: Status labels
---

## Work

:::requirement{#R1 depends-on=D2} A requirement with no status
REQ-NO-STATUS text.
:::

:::requirement{#R2 status=accepted} An accepted requirement
REQ-ACCEPTED text.
:::

:::assumption{#A1} An assumption nobody checked
ASSUMPTION text.
:::

## Rules

:::constraint{#C1 scope=document} A constraint with no level
CONSTRAINT text.
:::

:::constraint{#C2 scope=document level=should} A constraint that says should
SHOULD text.
:::

## Decisions

:::decision{#D1 status=superseded} The old choice
OLD-CHOICE text.
:::

:::decision{#D2 status=accepted supersedes=D1} The new choice
NEW-CHOICE text.
:::

## Filler

FILLER-ONE text that a small budget leaves out, written long enough to cost tokens on its own, so the budgeted read
has something it can omit without touching the rules or the requirements that the laws require.
